# M1 pipeline configuration demo. See README.md in this folder for getting an access token.
# Works with the VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client; Postman can import it.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# chainops_access cookie value from POST /auth/login (valid 10 minutes)
@token = paste-access-token-here
# A real project ID: select p.id, p.name from projects p;
@projectId = 05d2496e-5fa4-4d7a-9606-7dd98d154e4b

### Create (201; 409 if one already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Smart Contract CI","repository":"intelli-collective/vault-contracts","branch":"main","framework":"hardhat","stages":["compile","test","security"]}

### Read (200; 404 if not created yet)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update only the given fields (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"branch":"develop","stages":["checkout","compile","test","slither"]}

### Read again (200, shows the update)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid stage (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"stages":["deploy-mainnet"]}

### Missing token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/pipeline
